.TH MU2EDAQ-NOTIFY-DNS-UPDATE 1 "August 2026" "mu2edaq-notify 0.1.0" "Mu2e DAQ"
.SH NAME
mu2edaq\-notify\-dns\-update \- publish an EC2 instance's public IPv4 into Route 53
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B /usr/local/sbin/mu2edaq\-notify\-dns\-update
[\fB\-c\fR \fIFILE\fR]
[\fB\-z\fR \fIZONE_ID\fR]
[\fB\-r\fR \fIRECORD\fR]
[\fB\-t\fR \fISECONDS\fR]
[\fB\-i\fR \fIADDRESS\fR]
[\fB\-\-tries\fR \fIN\fR]
[\fB\-\-delay\fR \fISECONDS\fR]
[\fB\-\-wait\fR|\fB\-\-no\-wait\fR]
[\fB\-\-log\fR \fIFILE\fR]
[\fB\-n\fR]
[\fB\-q\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Runs
.I on
the mu2edaq\-notify AWS reverse\-proxy instance and points the proxy's public
.B A
record at whatever public IPv4 that instance currently holds.
.PP
It exists because the proxy no longer carries an Elastic IP. The instance is
normally stopped, its auto\-assigned public address is released on stop, and a
different one is attached on the next start, so the record has to follow the
instance rather than the instance being pinned to an address. The repo copy is
.IR scripts/aws\-notify\-dns\-update.sh ;
.BR install\-notify\-dns\-updater.sh (1)
puts it on the instance as
.IR /usr/local/sbin/mu2edaq\-notify\-dns\-update .
.PP
The address is read from IMDSv2
.RB ( public\-ipv4 ),
never from configuration, and is retried while it is still being attached. If
no address ever appears the run fails rather than publishing something wrong:
that state means the subnet is not auto\-assigning a public IPv4
.RB ( MapPublicIpOnLaunch )
and no address is attached to the interface.
.PP
The current record is read first, so a boot where nothing changed costs one
read and no write. Otherwise a single
.B UPSERT
is submitted and, by default, polled to
.BR INSYNC .
.SH OPTIONS
Precedence is command line, then environment, then the configuration file, then
built\-in defaults.
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-config " " \fIFILE\fR
Configuration file, sourced as shell. Default
.IR /etc/mu2edaq\-notify\-dns.conf .
.TP
.BR \-z ", " \-\-zone " " \fIZONE_ID\fR
Route 53 hosted zone. Default
.BR Z2OL4WKH228GKD .
.TP
.BR \-r ", " \-\-record " " \fIRECORD\fR
Record to maintain. Default
.BR notify.andrewnorman.org .
The IAM policy pins this name, so changing it needs a policy change too.
.TP
.BR \-t ", " \-\-ttl " " \fISECONDS\fR
Record TTL. Default 60, deliberately short because the address changes on
every start.
.TP
.BR \-i ", " \-\-ip " " \fIADDRESS\fR
Publish this address instead of asking IMDS. For recovery only.
.TP
.B \-\-tries \fIN\fR, \fB\-\-delay\fR \fISECONDS\fR
IMDS attempts and spacing while waiting for the public address. Default 30 and
2.
.TP
.BR \-\-wait ", " \-\-no\-wait
Wait, or do not wait, for the change to reach
.BR INSYNC .
Waiting is the default because the boot unit is ordered before
.BR caddy.service :
returning early would let Caddy attempt ACME validation against a record that
has not converged.
.TP
.BR \-\-log " " \fIFILE\fR
Also append output here. Empty disables. Default
.IR /var/log/mu2edaq\-notify\-dns.log .
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-dry\-run
Report the change, submit nothing.
.TP
.BR \-q ", " \-\-quiet
Only report changes and errors.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.B MU2EDAQ_NOTIFY_DNS_CONFIG,
.B MU2EDAQ_NOTIFY_ROUTE53_ZONE_ID,
.B MU2EDAQ_NOTIFY_DNS_RECORD,
.B MU2EDAQ_NOTIFY_DNS_TTL,
.B MU2EDAQ_NOTIFY_DNS_WAIT,
.B MU2EDAQ_NOTIFY_DNS_IP_TRIES,
.B MU2EDAQ_NOTIFY_DNS_IP_DELAY,
.B MU2EDAQ_NOTIFY_DNS_LOGFILE,
.B MU2EDAQ_NOTIFY_IMDS_BASE.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/mu2edaq-notify-dns.conf
Zone, record, TTL and retry budget.
.TP
.I /etc/systemd/system/mu2edaq-notify-dns.service
Runs this at every boot, ordered before
.BR caddy.service .
.TP
.I /etc/systemd/system/mu2edaq-notify-dns.timer
Five\-minute drift guard; a no\-op read when the record is already right.
.TP
.I /var/log/mu2edaq-notify-dns.log
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Record already correct, or updated.
.TP
.B 1
Failure: no IMDSv2 token, no public address, or a rejected Route 53 change.
.TP
.B 2
Usage error.
.SH EXAMPLES
Show what a run would do without touching Route 53:
.PP
.RS
.nf
sudo mu2edaq\-notify\-dns\-update \-\-dry\-run
.fi
.RE
.PP
Republish after an instance rebuild, without waiting for convergence:
.PP
.RS
.nf
sudo mu2edaq\-notify\-dns\-update \-\-no\-wait
journalctl \-u mu2edaq\-notify\-dns.service \-n 50 \-\-no\-pager
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR install-notify-dns-updater.sh (1),
.BR update-notify-dns.sh (1),
.BR update-notify-caa.sh (1),
.IR docs/reverse\-proxy\-setup.md ,
.IR docs/reverse\-proxy\-operations.md
